# Pencil design files are ENCRYPTED, and git must not pretend otherwise.
#
# `design/*.pen` is the canvas the whole product is drawn from. It is not text:
# git cannot diff it, and it absolutely cannot merge it. Left to its defaults git
# would happily attempt a three-way merge, produce a file that is neither
# designer's work, and hand back something Pencil then refuses to open — with the
# original of both sides already gone.
#
# `-merge` makes git STOP and say "both modified" instead. That is the correct
# outcome: somebody has to pick a side, reopen it in Pencil, and redo the losing
# change by hand. Loud and annoying beats silent and destroyed.
#
# WHICH MEANS: one person edits the canvas at a time. Say so in the channel
# before you start, and push as soon as you stop. See CONTRIBUTING.md
# §"Designers: working on the canvas".
*.pen binary -merge

# Brand assets — binary, diffable only as "changed".
design/brand/** binary

# Keep line endings sane for contributors on Windows (several of us are on WSL).
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
